# Sanctioned multi-write service functions: `path::function  N  reason`, where
# N is the exact write count (see scripts/check-single-write-service.sh).
# Each call site must be an exclusive branch or an idempotent retry, never two
# writes that both land for one logical change.
src/service/people.rs::set_member  3  exclusive match arms: remove OR set role
src/service/tasks/crud.rs::create_task_inner  2  if/else: signalled OR plain create
src/service/tasks/crud.rs::record_hook_event  4  exclusive match arms per hook kind
src/service/tasks/crud.rs::record_subagent_event  3  exclusive match arms per event
src/service/tasks/session.rs::report_rebase_done  3  one idempotent retry of the same report, or else one failure report (exclusive branches)
src/service/tasks/session.rs::report_session_done  2  one idempotent retry of the same report
# Added when the checker learned loops and `self.<helper>()` calls (G4). Counts are
# call sites summed through one level of helpers, so they move when a call is added.
src/service/learnings.rs::query_learnings  2  one best-effort telemetry write per returned learning, in a loop; a failed one only logs
src/service/tasks/crud.rs::create_task_signalled  2  delegates to create_task_inner (listed above): exclusive branches
src/service/tasks/crud.rs::create_task_returning  2  delegates to create_task_inner (listed above): exclusive branches
src/service/tasks/crud.rs::record_peer_message_sent  2  the sender's stamp, then a best-effort target stamp that only logs on failure; no half-change is observable
src/service/tasks/dispatch.rs::serve_dispatch_request  9  the claim, then exactly one terminal report on exclusive early-return branches; report_provisioned retries once, idempotently
src/service/tasks/session.rs::serve_rebase  8  exclusive terminal branches: one failure report, or one done report (itself listed above)
src/service/tasks/session.rs::serve_teardown  4  a done report or a failure report on exclusive branches; the early-return failure paths are exclusive too
